# Ollama Delegation Rule

When working in this repository, reduce hosted model usage by delegating suitable subtasks to local Ollama on the user's RTX 4090.

## Delegate To Local Ollama

- First drafts and rewrites for static HTML/CSS/JS content.
- Repetitive transformations (rename lists, mapping content blocks, template scaffolding).
- Summaries, extraction, and classification of local text/data files.
- Test-case or checklist generation where correctness can be verified afterward.
- Non-critical brainstorming where final decisions still stay with the primary agent.

Use:

```powershell
.\dev\ollama-delegate.ps1 -Prompt "<task>"
```

## Keep Cloud Models For

- Final decision-making with meaningful product/architecture trade-offs.
- Security-sensitive changes and auth/payment logic.
- Complex debugging with ambiguous root causes.
- Final quality checks for risky edits before completion.

## Performance Guardrails

- If local inference is slow or low quality, switch back to cloud immediately.
- Do not block user progress waiting on local generations for trivial gains.
- Keep outputs concise and verify any local output before applying to code.
